   8:     """
   9:     Simulate water pixels falling under gravity into basins formed by colored obstacles.
  10: 
  11:     Input structure:
  12:     - bg = 0. Water pixels = color 1 (blue).
  13:     - Other colors form static solid structures (walls, steps, containers).
  14:     - Water starts in unstable positions above or beside basins.
  15: 
  16:     Rule:
  17:     - Each water pixel falls straight down through bg cells.
  18:     - When blocked below, it slides diagonally through the unique open side cell.
  19:     - When resting on a surface, it slides horizontally toward the nearest gap where it can fall again.
  20:     - Process repeats until no water pixel moves.
  21: 
  22:     Key insight: Water seeks the deepest reachable basin via diagonal and horizontal sliding, not just vertical fall.
  23:     """
  24:     g = np.array(grid, dtype=int).copy()
  25:     H, W = g.shape
  26:     bg = 0
