  10: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  11:     """
  12:     Grow four clockwise spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross.
  13: 
  14:     Input structure:
  15:     - bg = 0 (black). A single teal (8) cross centered in the grid.
  16: 
  17:     Rule:
  18:     - Each arm tip launches a "turtle" heading 90° right of its outward direction.
  19:     - Movement priority: turn right > go straight > turn left (left only if not on border).
  20:     - Normal step = 2 cells; step right after a turn = 1 cell.
  21:     - Each new cell must have a 1-cell orthogonal gap from all existing walls except the predecessor.
  22: 
  23:     Key insight: The right-turn preference plus alternating 2/1 step lengths creates self-avoiding spirals that tile the grid with uniform spacing.
  24:     """
