 253:     """
 254:     Assemble colored rectangular sprites into a single tiled rectangle, anchored by a marker pixel.
 255: 
 256:     Input structure:
 257:     - bg = most common color. Several solid-colored rectangular sprites scattered on the grid.
 258:     - One sprite has a unique single-pixel marker (different color) at one corner — this is the anchor.
 259: 
 260:     Rule:
 261:     - Identify the anchor sprite (contains the marker pixel) and the remaining pieces.
 262:     - Rotate the anchor so the marker pixel lands at position (0,0) of the output.
 263:     - Pack all remaining pieces (allowing 90° rotations) to tile a complete rectangle with no gaps.
 264: 
 265:     Key insight: The lone marker pixel picks the anchor and fixes the output orientation — it must sit at the top-left corner.
 266:     """
 267:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
 268:     pieces, bg = _extract_pieces(g)
 269:     assert pieces, "grid has no non-background colors — input must contain colored pieces to assemble"
 270: 
